    {
      "section": "2.4",
      "label": "",
      "text": "The same applies to `ClearTextEncryptor` on the downlink.",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "2.4",
      "label": "",
      "text": "If a deployment needs additional SAs, override the `SdlsSaRouter` configuration (`SdlsCfg.SaMap`, `SdlsCfg.SaRouterPortCount`), connect the added router ports in the deployment topology, and ensure no map entry points at a `ClearText*` component (remap it to `UNCONNECTED` or remove it).",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "2.5",
      "label": "",
      "text": "Unmapped SAs are rejected (`UNKNOWN_SA`), so the map is the allow-list of acceptable SAs: keep it to exactly the SAs a deployment's real cryptographic components serve.",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "2.6",
      "label": "**Rate Groups:**",
      "text": "Connect a rate group to the **`comQueueRun`** (telemetry send rate) and **`aggregatorTimeout`** topology ports.",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "2.6",
      "label": "**Transport Endpoint:**",
      "text": "wire the ComStub ByteStream ports (variant A) or an external `Svc.ComInterface` (variant B) as documented in the usage note in `ComCcsdsSdls.fpp`.",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "2.6",
      "label": "",
      "text": "A deployment that selects a real crypto implementation (see 2.4) should give each router its own table via `SdlsSaRouter::configure()` (see the `SdlsSaRouterCfg.fpp` annotation), and adopts whatever setup that component requires — for the AES-GCM pair, a key source: `Svc.Ccsds.SdlsFileKeyManager` needs `configure(path, keySize)` before the first frame, and is not instantiated by this subtopology.",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "3",
      "label": "",
      "text": "`Svc.Ccsds.CcsdsSdlsFramer` prepends a 2-byte SA index to each aggregate, so projects must set `ComCcsdsConfig.Aggregator.aggregationSize = Svc.Ccsds.TmDataFieldSize - Svc.Ccsds.SdlsSaIndexSize` minus any per-frame overhead the encryptor adds, so that the encrypted aggregate plus the SA index fills the TM data field exactly.",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "3",
      "label": "",
      "text": "Because the TM frame is fixed-size, every encryptor reachable through the encryption SA router must produce the same output size.",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "3",
      "label": "",
      "text": "Projects selecting an encryptor with per-frame overhead should pin the fit next to the encryptor instance selection, e.g. `static_assert(ComCcsdsConfig::Aggregator::aggregationSize + Svc::Ccsds::SdlsSaIndexSize + 28 == Svc::Ccsds::TmDataFieldSize, \"...\")`.",
